meson-amvdec: AV1 on T7 - undo the word order of the RPM block

The T7 AV1 microcode stores the RPM parameter block with the order of every
group of four 16-bit words reversed (the vendor driver reverses it back when
it reads the block). Read at the S4 offsets, frame type, order hint and
height came out wrong (e.g. "firmware parsed type 0 hint 7 size 1920x1920,
controls 1 32 1920x1080"), and intra_only taken from the block would be
read from the wrong word.

Add an av1_rpm_swap platform capability, set for T7, and reverse the groups
after copying the block. Verified from dumps: after the swap type, order hint,
width and height match the V4L2 controls on every frame.
Needs 0007 applied.

